1
00:00:17,831 --> 00:00:20,301
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

2
00:00:23,531 --> 00:00:25,541
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

3
00:00:33,441 --> 00:00:34,981
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

4
00:00:54,901 --> 00:00:57,271
(Happy Anding)

5
00:00:57,271 --> 00:00:58,941
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

6
00:00:58,941 --> 00:01:00,171
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

7
00:01:00,171 --> 00:01:01,371
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

8
00:01:01,371 --> 00:01:02,571
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

9
00:01:02,571 --> 00:01:03,771
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

10
00:01:05,424 --> 00:01:06,624
This is only the beginning.

11
00:01:06,954 --> 00:01:08,264
You know Mi Kyeong's daughter, right?

12
00:01:08,594 --> 00:01:10,794
She was converted to a permanent hire...

13
00:01:10,964 --> 00:01:12,664
after just one year.

14
00:01:12,964 --> 00:01:14,634
That's easier said than done.

15
00:01:15,234 --> 00:01:17,264
That's why everyone calls it a miracle.

16
00:01:17,604 --> 00:01:19,204
Why couldn't it happen to you?

17
00:01:19,574 --> 00:01:21,874
Just act like you have nothing to lose...

18
00:01:22,204 --> 00:01:23,904
and hold out with a smile, no matter what.

19
00:01:24,174 --> 00:01:26,514
- Okay.
- Let's take the photo now.

20
00:01:26,574 --> 00:01:28,144
Mom, I have to go. I'll call you back.

21
00:01:33,954 --> 00:01:35,254
This is for your company ID, right?

22
00:01:36,354 --> 00:01:38,254
- Yes.
- Then I should make sure...

23
00:01:38,254 --> 00:01:39,824
it turns out extra nice.

24
00:01:39,924 --> 00:01:41,864
All right. Look straight ahead, please.

25
00:01:42,664 --> 00:01:43,694
Great.

26
00:01:44,394 --> 00:01:46,094
Every start is like that.

27
00:01:46,934 --> 00:01:49,104
A vague fear and excitement.

28
00:01:49,964 --> 00:01:51,234
It's complicated...

29
00:01:52,474 --> 00:01:53,774
yet full of hope.

30
00:01:54,374 --> 00:01:55,874
(Go Eun Young)

31
00:01:56,044 --> 00:01:57,044
However...

32
00:01:57,544 --> 00:01:59,074
- Eun Young.
- Yes?

33
00:02:01,244 --> 00:02:03,014
- Eun Young.
- Yes?

34
00:02:03,084 --> 00:02:05,914
- Are the materials ready yet?
- They're almost done.

35
00:02:11,494 --> 00:02:13,894
(Hyunsang Group Annual Import and Export Operations Plan)

36
00:02:16,994 --> 00:02:19,464
(By: Jeong Hye Min, Park Jin Ah, Kim Hyun Jung, Go Eun Young)

37
00:02:25,074 --> 00:02:27,874
The director was especially pleased with it.

38
00:02:28,104 --> 00:02:30,744
- I naturally came to realize...
- We'll treat you guys.

39
00:02:30,944 --> 00:02:32,244
Hyun Jung, can you book that rib place across the street?

40
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:33,744
- that I wasn't...
- Sure thing.

41
00:02:34,074 --> 00:02:37,284
- Everyone is coming, right?
- the one miracles happened to.

42
00:02:38,014 --> 00:02:40,154
When does the next temp start?

43
00:02:40,884 --> 00:02:42,384
No idea. They'll show up when it's time.

44
00:02:44,724 --> 00:02:47,154
At first, I blamed myself.

45
00:02:47,894 --> 00:02:51,064
That was the only way I could start over.

46
00:02:52,734 --> 00:02:54,094
Not being good at the job,

47
00:02:55,304 --> 00:02:56,934
lacking social skills...

48
00:02:58,004 --> 00:02:59,074
And...

49
00:03:00,234 --> 00:03:02,304
What else could there be?

50
00:03:10,144 --> 00:03:12,214
Just as I was growing numb...

51
00:03:12,214 --> 00:03:13,654
to the endless cycle of frustration...

52
00:03:16,824 --> 00:03:18,624
(Daeim International Co., Ltd. Go Eun Young)

53
00:03:19,694 --> 00:03:22,164
I'm Go Eun Young. It's a pleasure to meet you.

54
00:03:30,804 --> 00:03:32,074
Welcome.

55
00:03:35,544 --> 00:03:36,744
I met her.

56
00:03:38,174 --> 00:03:41,344
Could you make 30 copies of each of these, please?

57
00:03:41,344 --> 00:03:42,384
Sure.

58
00:03:42,784 --> 00:03:43,914
Where is the copier?

59
00:03:46,654 --> 00:03:48,184
(Kim Hee Jin: The copier is in front of the pantry.)

60
00:03:58,964 --> 00:04:00,664
(Kim Hee Jin: Want to grab lunch together?)

61
00:04:00,934 --> 00:04:02,734
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

62
00:04:03,064 --> 00:04:04,534
Relax and enjoy your lunch.

63
00:04:05,204 --> 00:04:08,074
Because I didn't invite you to lunch to evaluate you or anything.

64
00:04:09,244 --> 00:04:10,304
Got it?

65
00:04:11,244 --> 00:04:12,244
Yes.

66
00:04:12,374 --> 00:04:15,014
Honestly, I used to be a temp worker too.

67
00:04:16,644 --> 00:04:18,054
So I know exactly how you feel.

68
00:04:18,954 --> 00:04:21,154
An invisible ghost destined to vanish the moment the contract ends.

69
00:04:23,384 --> 00:04:24,724
Slack off, and they berate you.

70
00:04:25,524 --> 00:04:27,054
Work hard, and they berate you even more.

71
00:04:27,964 --> 00:04:29,194
You can never win.

72
00:04:30,464 --> 00:04:31,994
Corporate life is so rough.

73
00:04:33,164 --> 00:04:37,264
Earlier, when I saw you, walking in all shrunk and timid,

74
00:04:37,464 --> 00:04:38,904
it reminded me of how I used to be.

75
00:04:41,204 --> 00:04:43,174
Still, Eun Young, don't worry too much.

76
00:04:44,044 --> 00:04:45,414
I'll help you as much as I can.

77
00:04:46,814 --> 00:04:47,814
Okay?

78
00:04:49,044 --> 00:04:50,314
Let's make this work.

79
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,354
Shall we toast?

80
00:04:57,754 --> 00:05:00,194
- Great work, everyone. Cheers.
- Cheers. Good job, everyone.

81
00:05:01,124 --> 00:05:03,964
- Am I late? Sorry.
- What took you so long?

82
00:05:05,594 --> 00:05:06,694
Oh, Eun Young, you're here too?

83
00:05:06,834 --> 00:05:09,104
Yes. Isn't it for everyone, assistant managers and below?

84
00:05:09,564 --> 00:05:10,764
That includes Eun Young, doesn't it?

85
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:13,434
Oh. Right, of course.

86
00:05:13,804 --> 00:05:15,244
Come sit here, Eun Young.

87
00:05:15,744 --> 00:05:18,614
- Did he propose?
- Not yet.

88
00:05:18,774 --> 00:05:20,674
That's why I don't have a ring yet.

89
00:05:20,944 --> 00:05:22,014
He will soon.

90
00:05:22,184 --> 00:05:23,444
- Straighten up.
- Don't worry.

91
00:05:24,114 --> 00:05:26,714
- Right?
- He'd better.

92
00:05:27,614 --> 00:05:28,754
You must be so busy.

93
00:05:33,654 --> 00:05:34,664
What?

94
00:05:36,394 --> 00:05:37,564
When did I get in the car?

95
00:05:38,234 --> 00:05:39,434
Try to get some more sleep.

96
00:05:39,734 --> 00:05:42,064
It's still a ways to your place, Assistant Manager Kim.

97
00:05:44,574 --> 00:05:46,734
I told you to just call me Hee Jin when it was just the two of us.

98
00:05:49,504 --> 00:05:51,314
It still feels a little awkward for me.

99
00:05:57,784 --> 00:05:59,484
Eun Young, let me give you taxi fare.

100
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:01,684
No, really, it's fine. I can walk from here.

101
00:06:01,884 --> 00:06:04,184
- No, it's too far.
- Really, it's okay.

102
00:06:04,794 --> 00:06:07,894
Thank you so much for today.

103
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:10,594
See you tomorrow.

104
00:06:11,864 --> 00:06:12,864
Hee Jin.

105
00:06:17,464 --> 00:06:18,474
Eun Young.

106
00:06:21,944 --> 00:06:23,004
You know...

107
00:06:23,904 --> 00:06:26,974
that Taiwan export project I'm currently in charge of?

108
00:06:28,314 --> 00:06:29,484
Do you want to take it over?

109
00:06:34,754 --> 00:06:35,784
Me?

110
00:06:37,894 --> 00:06:39,324
I'll talk to the team leader.

111
00:06:39,954 --> 00:06:42,464
Putting your own name on a project...

112
00:06:42,464 --> 00:06:44,124
makes it much easier to land a full-time position.

113
00:06:44,634 --> 00:06:45,694
That's how it worked for me.

114
00:06:45,834 --> 00:06:47,164
You've got to make it this time.

115
00:06:48,304 --> 00:06:49,434
If only for your family.

116
00:06:51,304 --> 00:06:52,304
Right?

117
00:06:54,974 --> 00:06:55,974
Hee Jin.

118
00:07:03,944 --> 00:07:05,084
Thank you.

119
00:07:07,184 --> 00:07:08,254
You know,

120
00:07:09,224 --> 00:07:12,824
I used to think there were no such things as miracles in my life.

121
00:07:14,024 --> 00:07:15,494
But I was wrong.

122
00:07:16,424 --> 00:07:17,964
Meeting you...

123
00:07:19,294 --> 00:07:21,704
is the miracle in my life.

124
00:07:27,504 --> 00:07:28,504
A miracle?

125
00:07:30,974 --> 00:07:31,974
Same here.

126
00:07:32,574 --> 00:07:35,044
I'm so, so grateful that I met you, too, Eun Young.

127
00:07:37,714 --> 00:07:38,714
Get home safely.

128
00:07:40,314 --> 00:07:41,554
See you tomorrow.

129
00:07:50,164 --> 00:07:51,994
(Kim Hee Jin: Out of Office)

130
00:07:54,364 --> 00:07:57,334
(LODIAC Cosmetics Taiwan Action Plan Prepared by Go Eun Young)

131
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:05,074
Where is the desk for whoever is in charge...

132
00:08:05,074 --> 00:08:07,444
of LODIAC Cosmetics Taiwan exports?

133
00:08:09,184 --> 00:08:12,384
Yes, that's me. What can I do for you?

134
00:08:12,984 --> 00:08:15,654
So it's you.

135
00:08:18,724 --> 00:08:20,024
You wretched woman!

136
00:08:21,694 --> 00:08:22,694
Hey, you.

137
00:08:23,424 --> 00:08:26,794
All the goods are made, and now you decide to cancel the deal?

138
00:08:27,234 --> 00:08:29,934
I'm not letting you get away with this today.

139
00:08:31,804 --> 00:08:32,804
Get over here.

140
00:08:33,234 --> 00:08:35,104
- You... Let go.
- Sir, you can't do this here.

141
00:08:35,274 --> 00:08:36,674
Let go! Let me go now!

142
00:08:36,744 --> 00:08:37,744
- Let go!
- Let's step outside and talk.

143
00:08:37,804 --> 00:08:40,644
Let go, you bastards. Let go!

144
00:08:40,744 --> 00:08:43,414
What kind of nonsense is this? A double contract with our clients?

145
00:08:44,044 --> 00:08:46,684
Well, I'm not really sure...

146
00:08:47,014 --> 00:08:48,654
Aren't you the project manager?

147
00:08:49,884 --> 00:08:50,884
Well...

148
00:08:51,594 --> 00:08:54,494
They're threatening to sue us if we don't pay up immediately.

149
00:08:54,964 --> 00:08:57,394
Beg or do whatever to get this sorted out.

150
00:08:57,824 --> 00:08:58,894
Got it?

151
00:09:01,404 --> 00:09:02,604
What are you waiting for? Get moving.

152
00:09:02,864 --> 00:09:03,864
Yes, sir.

153
00:09:07,834 --> 00:09:10,004
They really should screen these contract workers better, darn it.

154
00:09:10,304 --> 00:09:11,614
Where do they find such trash...

155
00:09:13,114 --> 00:09:16,414
- Seriously. Out of the question.
- Sir. Please, sir.

156
00:09:16,444 --> 00:09:19,054
Please, give me a break. Please?

157
00:09:19,114 --> 00:09:20,284
Unbelievable!

158
00:09:20,914 --> 00:09:22,824
I'm about to die here. Who's supposed to save me?

159
00:09:23,224 --> 00:09:25,454
Because your company hasn't paid up,

160
00:09:25,794 --> 00:09:28,794
I can't even pay my workers, so I can't ship anything out.

161
00:09:28,864 --> 00:09:30,994
Do you see these boxes piling up or not?

162
00:09:31,964 --> 00:09:33,164
These? These right here?

163
00:09:33,434 --> 00:09:34,764
Do they just need to be moved right now?

164
00:09:35,104 --> 00:09:36,234
I'll move them.

165
00:09:40,174 --> 00:09:41,744
You've got to be kidding me.

166
00:10:17,174 --> 00:10:18,214
Exactly.

167
00:10:18,674 --> 00:10:20,014
So...

168
00:10:20,844 --> 00:10:23,984
She went all the way down to Cheonan just to clean up that mess?

169
00:10:24,044 --> 00:10:25,054
- Yes.
- Right.

170
00:10:25,254 --> 00:10:27,854
Poor thing. I feel bad for her.

171
00:10:27,854 --> 00:10:29,284
She brought it on herself.

172
00:10:29,484 --> 00:10:32,354
- Seriously...
- Doesn't Hee Jin creep you out?

173
00:10:32,854 --> 00:10:34,194
Telling her, "This is all for your own good,"

174
00:10:34,254 --> 00:10:36,364
gaslighting the naive girl to get her under her thumb,

175
00:10:36,794 --> 00:10:38,264
pretending to teach her the ropes...

176
00:10:38,264 --> 00:10:39,594
while dumping all her own work on her.

177
00:10:39,734 --> 00:10:41,034
And calling her to the team dinner...

178
00:10:41,034 --> 00:10:42,104
to make her the designated driver.

179
00:10:42,164 --> 00:10:43,634
She totally made her her chauffeur.

180
00:10:43,704 --> 00:10:47,104
And now she's even dumping projects she messed up on her.

181
00:10:47,474 --> 00:10:49,374
Then she calls in an out-of-office meeting...

182
00:10:49,404 --> 00:10:50,544
and ducks out completely.

183
00:10:51,274 --> 00:10:53,144
Well, that's how she survives.

184
00:10:53,514 --> 00:10:56,244
She knows how lonely and desperate those kids are,

185
00:10:56,244 --> 00:10:57,414
so she takes advantage of them.

186
00:10:58,154 --> 00:11:01,284
The idiot has no idea she's getting played.

187
00:11:01,584 --> 00:11:03,584
Show her a little kindness, and she gets so happy.

188
00:11:05,194 --> 00:11:06,424
Do you want to hear something crazy?

189
00:11:06,794 --> 00:11:07,794
What is it?

190
00:11:08,524 --> 00:11:09,994
She told Hee Jin...

191
00:11:10,994 --> 00:11:14,064
that she was her miracle.

192
00:11:14,334 --> 00:11:15,634
A miracle?

193
00:11:16,734 --> 00:11:18,374
What's wrong with her, seriously?

194
00:11:18,834 --> 00:11:20,234
Does she think she's living in some fairy tale?

195
00:11:20,434 --> 00:11:22,604
I'm actually starting to feel bad for her.

196
00:11:22,604 --> 00:11:23,704
Seriously, what a shame.

197
00:11:24,544 --> 00:11:25,944
She just picked the wrong person to trust.

198
00:11:33,884 --> 00:11:35,024
(Daeim International Co., Ltd.)

199
00:11:35,154 --> 00:11:36,154
Eun Young.

200
00:11:40,124 --> 00:11:41,864
I was out on business, so I just saw my phone.

201
00:11:42,924 --> 00:11:44,464
I heard something went wrong with the project.

202
00:11:46,634 --> 00:11:48,964
Why did things have to blow up when I was out on field work?

203
00:11:51,934 --> 00:11:56,504
Meeting you is the miracle in my life.

204
00:11:57,944 --> 00:11:59,074
Same here.

205
00:11:59,514 --> 00:12:02,344
I'm so, so grateful that I met you, too, Eun Young.

206
00:12:06,114 --> 00:12:07,354
Are you okay?

207
00:12:07,984 --> 00:12:09,454
You're not hurt, right?

208
00:12:13,294 --> 00:12:14,354
Let me see.

209
00:12:41,654 --> 00:12:43,284
(Mom)

210
00:12:43,424 --> 00:12:45,024
(Call me when you're off work.)

211
00:12:45,094 --> 00:12:46,794
(Your father is driving me crazy.)

212
00:12:46,854 --> 00:12:50,464
What really made me feel pathetic back then...

213
00:12:52,494 --> 00:12:54,294
was that I lacked the courage to quit.

214
00:12:55,804 --> 00:12:58,404
It was just myself.

215
00:12:59,274 --> 00:13:01,704
How long is she going to hang on like that?

216
00:13:01,844 --> 00:13:03,174
She'll hear you.

217
00:13:03,674 --> 00:13:04,914
No, she won't.

218
00:13:04,974 --> 00:13:06,774
Even if she does, what's she going to do about it?

219
00:13:07,744 --> 00:13:10,244
Want to bet on when she'll quit?

220
00:13:10,784 --> 00:13:12,354
I tried to hang in there.

221
00:13:14,924 --> 00:13:16,684
I really tried, but...

222
00:13:22,224 --> 00:13:23,994
I love it. I love it so much.

223
00:13:24,594 --> 00:13:25,634
Mom.

224
00:13:27,564 --> 00:13:28,634
I'm sorry.

225
00:13:34,534 --> 00:13:35,774
For me,

226
00:13:37,974 --> 00:13:39,774
I guess that wasn't the answer.

227
00:14:23,254 --> 00:14:25,224
A year passed after that.

228
00:14:27,954 --> 00:14:29,294
(Daeim International Co., Ltd. Kim Hee Jin)

229
00:14:29,364 --> 00:14:31,094
I thought I had forgotten.

230
00:14:32,294 --> 00:14:36,004
Or at least, I thought I was moving on.

231
00:14:36,634 --> 00:14:38,974
Do you work here?

232
00:14:44,204 --> 00:14:46,714
Well, see you around, Eun Young.

233
00:14:49,214 --> 00:14:51,544
- How do you know her?
- Well, the thing is...

234
00:14:56,124 --> 00:14:58,594
- We've arrived, Madam President.
- Hello.

235
00:15:11,434 --> 00:15:12,434
What's wrong?

236
00:15:14,834 --> 00:15:16,004
Are you in pain?

237
00:15:28,184 --> 00:15:29,184
Eun Young?

238
00:15:45,974 --> 00:15:53,444
(Episode 6: Just for One Person)

239
00:16:02,584 --> 00:16:03,984
I'm coming in.

240
00:16:06,354 --> 00:16:09,494
It's so stuffy in here.

241
00:16:10,064 --> 00:16:11,964
It's like a haunted house.

242
00:16:13,094 --> 00:16:15,434
The weather is so nice. Look outside, Eun Young.

243
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:18,674
It's so clear. It's perfect for a picnic.

244
00:16:21,234 --> 00:16:22,244
Seriously?

245
00:16:22,304 --> 00:16:24,504
You're making me feel bad for even bringing you food.

246
00:16:24,804 --> 00:16:26,114
I'm heading to my part-time job,

247
00:16:26,114 --> 00:16:28,414
so please eat at least a spoonful of this while I'm gone.

248
00:16:41,324 --> 00:16:43,064
This character is better than that one.

249
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:45,194
It'll be much easier to connect with the audience later.

250
00:16:45,334 --> 00:16:46,934
And it's easier for me to act out, too.

251
00:16:48,704 --> 00:16:49,704
Hey.

252
00:16:50,604 --> 00:16:51,734
What?

253
00:16:51,974 --> 00:16:53,074
Let's go with this one.

254
00:16:53,604 --> 00:16:55,774
- Okay.
- I'm here.

255
00:16:55,874 --> 00:16:57,274
Hey, you made it?

256
00:16:57,344 --> 00:16:59,174
How is Eun Young? Still the same?

257
00:17:00,374 --> 00:17:02,444
- Yes.
- Hasn't it been two weeks already?

258
00:17:03,414 --> 00:17:04,744
Does she sleep at night?

259
00:17:05,714 --> 00:17:07,714
She's not eating or sleeping.

260
00:17:08,214 --> 00:17:09,624
She just stays in bed.

261
00:17:10,724 --> 00:17:12,194
Everything will be all right.

262
00:17:12,654 --> 00:17:13,654
Of course.

263
00:17:14,424 --> 00:17:15,494
Did you eat?

264
00:17:16,964 --> 00:17:18,194
You skipped your meal again, didn't you?

265
00:17:18,194 --> 00:17:19,494
- Jun Seo.
- Yes?

266
00:17:19,494 --> 00:17:22,634
- Make a rice bowl, please.
- No, really, I'm not hungry.

267
00:17:23,034 --> 00:17:25,334
Give me that. Go sit down.

268
00:17:28,204 --> 00:17:29,444
Eat up.

269
00:17:36,944 --> 00:17:38,954
It's more serious than I thought.

270
00:17:39,654 --> 00:17:41,054
Not like we ever had fans anyway.

271
00:17:41,284 --> 00:17:43,124
Having one and then not feels so empty.

272
00:17:47,594 --> 00:17:48,694
I should get going.

273
00:17:48,694 --> 00:17:51,364
Hey, let's finish up later at home.

274
00:17:52,364 --> 00:17:53,894
Hang in there, Ji Young.

275
00:17:55,234 --> 00:17:56,604
- Bye.
- See you, Mr. Jung.

276
00:17:56,664 --> 00:17:57,664
All right.

277
00:18:00,834 --> 00:18:02,074
Still?

278
00:18:03,474 --> 00:18:04,474
What happened?

279
00:18:05,474 --> 00:18:06,544
Is she still not talking?

280
00:18:07,144 --> 00:18:09,484
Her sister is trying her best,

281
00:18:10,044 --> 00:18:15,014
but she bottled up so much pain that it seems hard to let it out.

282
00:18:17,754 --> 00:18:18,824
Really?

283
00:18:23,724 --> 00:18:24,864
Don't ever do that.

284
00:18:28,364 --> 00:18:29,634
When things get tough, say it's tough.

285
00:18:29,704 --> 00:18:32,274
When you're hurting, say it hurts. You have to tell me right away.

286
00:18:32,834 --> 00:18:33,834
Got it?

287
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:36,004
Of course.

288
00:18:37,944 --> 00:18:41,714
To begin with, I'm not as nice as Eun Young.

289
00:18:42,384 --> 00:18:44,284
You know what happened in high school...

290
00:18:44,344 --> 00:18:46,114
to that upperclassman at cram school...

291
00:18:46,354 --> 00:18:48,454
who bullied me.

292
00:18:48,584 --> 00:18:51,254
That's why to this day I've never dared to cross you.

293
00:18:52,324 --> 00:18:53,454
Look at you.

294
00:18:56,794 --> 00:18:57,794
Right.

295
00:18:58,464 --> 00:19:01,334
I told you I have a conference this weekend, right?

296
00:19:01,634 --> 00:19:02,634
Yes.

297
00:19:02,704 --> 00:19:06,174
Well, my colleague and I suddenly have to present together,

298
00:19:06,504 --> 00:19:08,704
so we're pulling all-nighters starting today.

299
00:19:11,344 --> 00:19:13,914
I don't think I can see you at all this week.

300
00:19:15,044 --> 00:19:16,044
Sorry.

301
00:19:17,044 --> 00:19:18,314
It's work. Why be sorry?

302
00:19:19,454 --> 00:19:22,384
Still, those jerks gave you zero notice?

303
00:19:22,384 --> 00:19:23,654
Making you suffer.

304
00:19:23,824 --> 00:19:25,554
When they say jump, I have to jump.

305
00:19:31,364 --> 00:19:32,364
Hey.

306
00:19:34,694 --> 00:19:36,004
Already?

307
00:19:36,504 --> 00:19:38,234
Okay, got it. I'll be right out.

308
00:19:39,374 --> 00:19:41,534
Sorry, I have to go. My colleague is here.

309
00:19:41,704 --> 00:19:43,444
We're heading out to do some research.

310
00:19:43,504 --> 00:19:45,074
Finish your food before you go, okay?

311
00:19:45,844 --> 00:19:47,444
Let's walk out together. I'm done.

312
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:48,714
Are you sure? You don't want any more?

313
00:19:48,784 --> 00:19:49,784
I'm good.

314
00:19:56,824 --> 00:19:57,884
You made it?

315
00:19:58,724 --> 00:20:00,394
Hello. Good to see you again.

316
00:20:00,924 --> 00:20:01,924
Hello.

317
00:20:02,794 --> 00:20:04,924
- So Tae Hoon was your colleague.
- Yes.

318
00:20:05,164 --> 00:20:06,164
Where are you headed?

319
00:20:06,234 --> 00:20:08,064
If you're going to the subway, I can give you a ride.

320
00:20:08,264 --> 00:20:10,004
Yes, sweetie. It's hot out.

321
00:20:10,364 --> 00:20:12,974
Oh, no, it's fine. I have somewhere to be,

322
00:20:13,034 --> 00:20:14,634
so I can just walk that way.

323
00:20:15,874 --> 00:20:16,874
Hang in there today, babe.

324
00:20:17,544 --> 00:20:19,014
Make sure you eat, even if you're busy.

325
00:20:19,114 --> 00:20:20,114
Okay.

326
00:20:21,344 --> 00:20:23,284
- Please take good care of Na Yeon.
- Sure.

327
00:20:32,154 --> 00:20:34,594
- What's his deal?
- He's in good shape.

328
00:20:36,264 --> 00:20:37,764
- See you again.
- Yes.

329
00:20:37,824 --> 00:20:38,834
Let's go.

330
00:20:39,434 --> 00:20:41,334
I'll call you. Go on.

331
00:20:43,234 --> 00:20:44,734
- Have a good one.
- Yes.

332
00:20:59,984 --> 00:21:01,084
Look at this punk.

333
00:21:02,154 --> 00:21:03,354
What's with the swagger?

334
00:21:03,584 --> 00:21:05,354
Does he go to work just to show off his watch?

335
00:21:05,424 --> 00:21:06,424
That little punk.

336
00:21:08,424 --> 00:21:09,424
Darn it.

337
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:37,754
Let's see.

338
00:21:55,744 --> 00:21:57,804
(Can a fan club president really stay away this long?)

339
00:21:57,874 --> 00:22:00,744
(We wrote a killer new sketch. Aren't you even curious?)

340
00:22:11,784 --> 00:22:15,424
(If you don't reply right now, you'll lose your title for good!)

341
00:22:28,204 --> 00:22:29,774
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

342
00:22:29,844 --> 00:22:30,844
Thank you.

343
00:22:40,514 --> 00:22:42,254
Mom, I'm at work.

344
00:22:43,254 --> 00:22:45,694
Eun Young? She went for corporate training.

345
00:22:45,754 --> 00:22:47,054
You can't answer calls when you're in training.

346
00:22:47,754 --> 00:22:50,064
It's good she's busy. Why be like that?

347
00:22:50,364 --> 00:22:52,934
She's not a child. You know no news is good news.

348
00:22:57,304 --> 00:22:58,304
You're where?

349
00:22:59,834 --> 00:23:00,834
Oh, really?

350
00:23:01,374 --> 00:23:02,374
Leaving me on read?

351
00:23:03,644 --> 00:23:04,674
Come on.

352
00:23:08,674 --> 00:23:09,684
Darn it.

353
00:23:12,914 --> 00:23:14,684
- Hello?
- Sir, please hurry.

354
00:23:14,754 --> 00:23:16,484
Where are you right now, Tae Gu?

355
00:23:19,254 --> 00:23:21,554
In front of your house. Why?

356
00:23:50,124 --> 00:23:51,124
Get up.

357
00:23:59,464 --> 00:24:01,234
We have to leave right now. Your mom says she's coming.

358
00:24:06,274 --> 00:24:07,374
Stay out of it.

359
00:24:11,744 --> 00:24:12,774
Get up, hurry.

360
00:24:14,014 --> 00:24:15,584
I told you to stay out of it.

361
00:24:22,724 --> 00:24:24,054
I'm warning you.

362
00:24:28,294 --> 00:24:29,294
What's wrong with you?

363
00:24:30,124 --> 00:24:32,464
What are you doing? Let go.

364
00:24:34,194 --> 00:24:36,734
Let go. What do you think you're doing?

365
00:24:37,204 --> 00:24:39,674
- Let go.
- I'm coming to bring dishes...

366
00:24:39,734 --> 00:24:42,844
to my own daughter's place, and I need permission first?

367
00:24:43,674 --> 00:24:47,514
Forget it. What do you mean, grab coffee?

368
00:24:47,574 --> 00:24:48,644
I told you, I'm already here.

369
00:24:49,214 --> 00:24:51,884
What's wrong with you, seriously? Hang up.

370
00:24:52,254 --> 00:24:54,514
It's boiling hot out, and she keeps babbling.

371
00:24:59,254 --> 00:25:01,754
What on earth is that smell?

372
00:25:01,994 --> 00:25:03,694
They could at least air the place out.

373
00:25:05,834 --> 00:25:09,804
What do they even cook and eat here? What do these girls live on?

374
00:25:11,164 --> 00:25:12,804
Mom.

375
00:25:12,874 --> 00:25:15,104
Why show up out of nowhere without calling?

376
00:25:15,174 --> 00:25:16,444
What are you doing here?

377
00:25:16,504 --> 00:25:18,044
Your sister hasn't answered her phone,

378
00:25:18,044 --> 00:25:19,744
so I got worried and came by.

379
00:25:20,144 --> 00:25:21,144
I just wanted to see her face,

380
00:25:21,214 --> 00:25:22,444
and now you're saying she's gone too.

381
00:25:22,914 --> 00:25:26,514
Hey, nothing is really wrong with your sister, right?

382
00:25:26,914 --> 00:25:28,554
I told you there was nothing.

383
00:25:28,554 --> 00:25:29,784
How many times do I have to tell you?

384
00:25:30,324 --> 00:25:33,024
Why did you make so much food again? It won't even all fit in the fridge.

385
00:25:33,094 --> 00:25:36,424
Hey! Leave that one out and eat it once it ripens.

386
00:25:36,924 --> 00:25:40,064
And this one tastes best if you eat it today.

387
00:25:40,134 --> 00:25:41,934
Honestly, it breaks my heart.

388
00:25:50,544 --> 00:25:52,774
Are you all washed up? Come sit down.

389
00:25:52,974 --> 00:25:55,444
Mom made a whole bunch of your favorite side dishes.

390
00:25:56,044 --> 00:25:58,384
She always goes completely overboard.

391
00:25:58,784 --> 00:26:00,184
Where are you going now?

392
00:26:01,214 --> 00:26:02,424
Look, ta-da.

393
00:26:02,754 --> 00:26:04,184
She even made the meat patties you love.

394
00:26:05,454 --> 00:26:06,454
I'm tired.

395
00:26:06,824 --> 00:26:07,824
Wait a second.

396
00:26:08,154 --> 00:26:11,964
Mom was up at dawn making this just for you.

397
00:26:12,334 --> 00:26:14,064
- Just eat one bite.
- I told you I don't want it.

398
00:26:14,134 --> 00:26:16,634
- Just one bite. Just one.
- I said no!

399
00:26:33,654 --> 00:26:34,854
You just go back in there?

400
00:26:37,854 --> 00:26:39,394
Does running away in there fix anything?

401
00:26:42,564 --> 00:26:45,124
Just how long are you going to hide inside that tiny room?

402
00:26:49,134 --> 00:26:50,134
Eun Young.

403
00:26:53,204 --> 00:26:54,674
Who cares about those people?

404
00:26:56,744 --> 00:26:58,474
Are they going to eat you alive?

405
00:27:00,144 --> 00:27:01,344
Will they?

406
00:27:03,644 --> 00:27:06,554
At least tell me what happened so I know what's going on.

407
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:11,254
Don't go in.

408
00:27:13,194 --> 00:27:14,594
I told you not to go in.

409
00:27:20,194 --> 00:27:21,194
Come out.

410
00:27:21,634 --> 00:27:23,534
- What's wrong with you?
- Come out.

411
00:27:23,604 --> 00:27:25,304
- What's wrong with you?
- Come out.

412
00:27:25,364 --> 00:27:28,334
What's wrong with you? Seriously, what's gotten into you?

413
00:27:28,974 --> 00:27:30,804
- Let's go.
- What are you doing?

414
00:27:30,874 --> 00:27:32,674
- Ji Young.
- I said let's go.

415
00:27:32,744 --> 00:27:35,074
Ji Young, seriously, stop this.

416
00:27:35,144 --> 00:27:37,784
- Get up, let's go.
- What are you doing?

417
00:27:46,594 --> 00:27:48,754
- What's gotten into you?
- Let's go.

418
00:27:48,754 --> 00:27:49,894
Let's go!

419
00:27:49,964 --> 00:27:53,194
- Let's go, Eun Young. Come on.
- What's going on? Hold on.

420
00:27:53,864 --> 00:27:56,104
Let's just go. Whether it's to the hospital...

421
00:27:56,164 --> 00:27:58,464
or to kill the bastards who hurt you.

422
00:27:59,134 --> 00:28:02,034
Let's do something so you can live like a human being!

423
00:28:02,474 --> 00:28:04,974
Ji Young, why don't we calm down?

424
00:28:22,494 --> 00:28:24,024
You don't think about me at all, do you?

425
00:28:25,834 --> 00:28:28,664
It's already been a year being stuck at your side.

426
00:28:29,734 --> 00:28:31,104
Cleaning up your messes...

427
00:28:31,164 --> 00:28:32,704
is driving me insane. Do you know that?

428
00:28:35,434 --> 00:28:37,704
Eun Young.

429
00:28:38,104 --> 00:28:40,144
Look at the state you're in.

430
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:44,284
It's pathetic. You're pathetic!

431
00:28:47,114 --> 00:28:49,384
What on earth is so hard and painful?

432
00:28:51,384 --> 00:28:53,524
It's all in the past anyway, isn't it?

433
00:28:53,754 --> 00:28:55,224
- What's so hard?
- Ji Young.

434
00:28:55,294 --> 00:28:56,864
- Say something.
- Calm down.

435
00:28:57,894 --> 00:28:59,394
Let's go inside, okay?

436
00:29:15,644 --> 00:29:16,644
Fine, I'm sorry.

437
00:29:25,154 --> 00:29:27,694
I'm sorry I can't live brainlessly like you.

438
00:29:29,394 --> 00:29:30,964
I'm truly sorry.

439
00:29:37,104 --> 00:29:40,104
Was I really holding you back?

440
00:29:42,544 --> 00:29:43,544
No, I wasn't.

441
00:29:44,444 --> 00:29:47,674
You're using me as an excuse to stall for time.

442
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:48,814
It's because you...

443
00:29:50,414 --> 00:29:53,054
lack the courage to face your own dreams.

444
00:29:57,154 --> 00:29:58,384
It's not that you won't.

445
00:30:01,394 --> 00:30:02,664
It's that you're afraid you can't.

446
00:30:22,144 --> 00:30:23,144
You're right.

447
00:30:24,514 --> 00:30:25,814
You nailed it.

448
00:30:26,854 --> 00:30:29,324
I can't even take care of myself,

449
00:30:29,924 --> 00:30:32,254
so having to watch you whine...

450
00:30:35,654 --> 00:30:37,394
is so suffocating that I can't do this anymore.

451
00:30:38,394 --> 00:30:39,994
I'll get out of your hair like you wanted,

452
00:30:39,994 --> 00:30:41,394
so live like that all by yourself...

453
00:30:42,634 --> 00:30:43,904
in that cramped room all alone...

454
00:30:45,434 --> 00:30:46,804
for the rest of your life,

455
00:30:48,934 --> 00:30:50,604
harping on about your old wounds.

456
00:30:55,574 --> 00:30:56,844
- Ji Young.
- Hey...

457
00:31:26,614 --> 00:31:28,344
Take it easy on the drinking.

458
00:31:32,114 --> 00:31:33,454
I have no regrets.

459
00:31:34,054 --> 00:31:35,184
Did anyone say you did?

460
00:31:36,884 --> 00:31:39,724
Honestly, I felt so suffocated,

461
00:31:41,224 --> 00:31:42,724
but now I feel completely relieved.

462
00:31:42,794 --> 00:31:45,124
Now I can finally sleep with my mind at ease.

463
00:31:51,164 --> 00:31:53,834
What? Why are you looking at me like that?

464
00:31:55,474 --> 00:31:58,904
Look, I actually held out for a really long time.

465
00:31:59,444 --> 00:32:01,574
We were never compatible to begin with.

466
00:32:02,514 --> 00:32:05,684
We're just too different. It's obvious, isn't it?

467
00:32:05,744 --> 00:32:09,554
My sister is meek and clueless,

468
00:32:09,784 --> 00:32:12,584
while I'm all bubbly and cute.

469
00:32:13,454 --> 00:32:14,524
My sister is like an ant...

470
00:32:15,354 --> 00:32:18,724
whose entire identity is about responsibility,

471
00:32:18,824 --> 00:32:23,364
while I'm like a grasshopper who avoids anything stressful...

472
00:32:23,434 --> 00:32:25,104
because you only live once.

473
00:32:28,234 --> 00:32:29,744
You know what's funny?

474
00:32:31,644 --> 00:32:33,444
Guess what excuse...

475
00:32:33,674 --> 00:32:36,944
I used the most with my parents when I was little?

476
00:32:38,584 --> 00:32:40,554
"You have Eun Young."

477
00:32:41,084 --> 00:32:44,954
"She'll be a success, so it's fine if I slack off, right?"

478
00:32:47,754 --> 00:32:48,754
That was how...

479
00:32:49,424 --> 00:32:51,524
I avoided my parents' expectations...

480
00:32:52,064 --> 00:32:53,664
and becoming an adult.

481
00:32:54,294 --> 00:32:55,664
I avoided all of it,

482
00:32:57,434 --> 00:32:58,604
hiding behind my sister...

483
00:32:59,504 --> 00:33:01,474
and using her as a human shield.

484
00:33:03,674 --> 00:33:06,674
I knew it was burdening her more and more,

485
00:33:07,274 --> 00:33:08,614
but I pretended not to notice.

486
00:33:10,314 --> 00:33:11,544
I thought,

487
00:33:11,944 --> 00:33:13,754
"Well, it's because she's foolishly nice,"

488
00:33:13,814 --> 00:33:15,184
"so it's not my fault."

489
00:33:16,254 --> 00:33:18,554
Right? Aren't I right?

490
00:33:18,984 --> 00:33:21,394
It's all because Go Eun Young is an idiot.

491
00:33:21,454 --> 00:33:22,494
It's not because I...

492
00:33:22,964 --> 00:33:23,964
I...

493
00:33:30,604 --> 00:33:31,864
It's not because I...

494
00:33:40,014 --> 00:33:41,674
She's just so kind and gentle...

495
00:33:45,484 --> 00:33:47,054
She endured it until...

496
00:33:49,454 --> 00:33:50,954
she ended up like this, didn't she?

497
00:34:10,144 --> 00:34:12,704
What am I doing? I must be losing my mind.

498
00:34:14,244 --> 00:34:15,344
I'm sorry.

499
00:34:15,874 --> 00:34:18,014
Whenever I drink beer, I get like this.

500
00:34:19,414 --> 00:34:23,224
I'm going to run and pee real quick, so just stay right there.

501
00:34:29,964 --> 00:34:32,524
Both of them are too good for this world.

502
00:34:33,934 --> 00:34:35,564
What are we going to do with these sisters?

503
00:34:38,034 --> 00:34:39,034
(Enjoy Whatever Comes)

504
00:34:39,104 --> 00:34:40,104
(Life Is Bittersweet)

505
00:34:42,004 --> 00:34:43,004
I'm sorry.

506
00:34:43,074 --> 00:34:45,104
Once I start, I just can't stop.

507
00:34:48,374 --> 00:34:49,884
You should've knocked.

508
00:35:00,594 --> 00:35:04,164
Darn it. Look at my tears.

509
00:35:35,754 --> 00:35:37,264
I thought she might starve,

510
00:35:37,324 --> 00:35:39,494
so I barely got her to eat a bite of rice with seaweed soup.

511
00:35:39,494 --> 00:35:40,934
(Sleep: Went to bed at 10pm. Tossed and turned until 3am.)

512
00:35:40,934 --> 00:35:42,564
(Woke up at 11am the next day)

513
00:35:42,564 --> 00:35:43,804
(Medication: Morning medication...)

514
00:35:43,804 --> 00:35:46,164
I need to help her keep a regular sleep schedule,

515
00:35:46,234 --> 00:35:47,874
but is that truly impossible?

516
00:35:48,434 --> 00:35:50,544
She barely fell asleep, so I can't wake her.

517
00:35:55,074 --> 00:35:56,844
Another day without even drinking enough water.

518
00:35:57,414 --> 00:36:00,814
She barely speaks and just spaces out all day.

519
00:36:01,414 --> 00:36:04,684
What could she be thinking? She won't answer even when I ask.

520
00:36:05,054 --> 00:36:06,624
(Salmon Avocado Rice Bowl)

521
00:36:06,694 --> 00:36:08,394
A recipe to beat depression.

522
00:36:08,454 --> 00:36:10,894
(Salmon, Avocado, Scallion, Onion, Egg Yolk, Rice, Soy Sauce)

523
00:36:10,964 --> 00:36:14,564
Got this recipe from Man Sik, and she ate it all. Total success.

524
00:36:14,634 --> 00:36:15,894
(She ate it all. Success.)

525
00:36:19,934 --> 00:36:21,374
(Drag her out for a walk every day, even by force.)

526
00:36:21,434 --> 00:36:22,674
(Get some sun and exercise, like a human.)

527
00:36:22,734 --> 00:36:24,074
(Anxiety and stress keep the mind from settling down.)

528
00:36:24,074 --> 00:36:26,714
(Eun Young and Ji Young can do this. We'll overcome it.)

529
00:36:31,114 --> 00:36:36,424
(Eun Young and Ji Young can do this. We'll overcome it.)

530
00:37:39,014 --> 00:37:43,524
(Mexapro: One Tablet Daily, Insomnia)

531
00:37:55,294 --> 00:37:56,304
Hello.

532
00:37:57,804 --> 00:37:58,804
Hi.

533
00:38:02,204 --> 00:38:03,974
Hyun Gu, is this the right medication?

534
00:38:04,374 --> 00:38:05,604
It looks a bit different from last...

535
00:38:08,574 --> 00:38:11,414
Hey, say hello. She's the one who helped me last...

536
00:38:18,324 --> 00:38:19,324
Wait, do you know each other?

537
00:38:34,374 --> 00:38:39,204
Gosh, what a crazy coincidence. How do you two keep crossing paths?

538
00:38:41,144 --> 00:38:42,144
I know.

539
00:38:42,814 --> 00:38:44,314
We just keep running into each other.

540
00:38:45,084 --> 00:38:47,684
Her vibe seemed completely different from when I saw her before.

541
00:38:48,754 --> 00:38:49,854
Did something happen?

542
00:38:50,984 --> 00:38:51,984
Do you know?

543
00:38:53,824 --> 00:38:54,824
No.

544
00:38:55,694 --> 00:38:56,864
I don't know either.

545
00:39:01,964 --> 00:39:03,434
Are you two really close?

546
00:39:04,764 --> 00:39:05,864
Are we close?

547
00:39:06,904 --> 00:39:08,134
She's just a woman who lives in the next villa.

548
00:39:09,074 --> 00:39:10,104
And our fan.

549
00:39:11,344 --> 00:39:12,404
A fan?

550
00:39:13,114 --> 00:39:14,174
What else?

551
00:39:14,174 --> 00:39:15,414
- What?
- What?

552
00:39:16,514 --> 00:39:19,014
Nothing, that's all.

553
00:39:20,614 --> 00:39:21,854
That's all?

554
00:39:27,794 --> 00:39:29,494
What else would there be?

555
00:39:33,764 --> 00:39:34,894
Turn right at the intersection.

556
00:39:35,294 --> 00:39:36,564
You said you need to get your wheelchair fixed.

557
00:39:36,804 --> 00:39:38,964
- The shop is that way.
- Forget it. I'm going home.

558
00:39:39,564 --> 00:39:41,604
Why? We're already out. Let's just go.

559
00:39:42,204 --> 00:39:44,604
Your mind is completely elsewhere.

560
00:39:45,404 --> 00:39:46,774
I'm really fine,

561
00:39:47,344 --> 00:39:48,814
so drop me off and get going.

562
00:39:53,954 --> 00:39:56,624
(Hyujung Mental Health Clinic)

563
00:40:00,554 --> 00:40:01,724
Man, it's boiling hot.

564
00:40:05,664 --> 00:40:06,834
Do you want to get some ice cream?

565
00:40:36,094 --> 00:40:37,094
No, it's okay.

566
00:40:37,864 --> 00:40:40,194
Hold on. I can't return them anyway.

567
00:40:49,174 --> 00:40:50,174
There.

568
00:40:51,004 --> 00:40:52,374
Gosh.

569
00:40:53,344 --> 00:40:54,844
Where else would you get fan service like this?

570
00:41:00,584 --> 00:41:01,584
Here,

571
00:41:02,554 --> 00:41:03,554
take your pick.

572
00:41:04,154 --> 00:41:05,224
Strawberry or vanilla.

573
00:41:10,664 --> 00:41:11,864
I like strawberry too.

574
00:41:53,004 --> 00:41:55,204
I seem strange, don't I?

575
00:42:02,944 --> 00:42:04,114
I know.

576
00:42:05,984 --> 00:42:08,014
I don't even understand myself,

577
00:42:10,524 --> 00:42:12,484
so how could anyone else?

578
00:42:16,824 --> 00:42:18,024
Like Ji Young said,

579
00:42:18,864 --> 00:42:20,464
it's all in the past.

580
00:42:22,994 --> 00:42:24,404
Those people...

581
00:42:27,974 --> 00:42:29,034
are probably out there, smiling,

582
00:42:29,874 --> 00:42:31,544
living their best lives.

583
00:42:36,814 --> 00:42:37,884
So why only me?

584
00:42:46,754 --> 00:42:49,724
I don't know why I'm like this either.

585
00:43:03,944 --> 00:43:05,574
My brother suffers from phantom pain.

586
00:43:07,574 --> 00:43:10,044
You know what's so crazy about phantom pain?

587
00:43:10,914 --> 00:43:12,944
Even though he lost his leg 20 years ago,

588
00:43:14,714 --> 00:43:16,984
it hurts like it was just injured.

589
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:20,454
To other people, it's a wound from the past,

590
00:43:22,824 --> 00:43:24,364
but to my brother, it's happening right now.

591
00:43:29,194 --> 00:43:31,064
No matter how much time has passed,

592
00:43:34,474 --> 00:43:36,474
whether you can see it or not,

593
00:43:39,974 --> 00:43:41,514
pain is still pain.

594
00:43:45,744 --> 00:43:47,184
If it hurts, it hurts.

595
00:43:48,414 --> 00:43:49,414
What else can you do?

596
00:43:57,064 --> 00:43:58,094
People...

597
00:43:59,294 --> 00:44:00,294
terrify me.

598
00:44:06,204 --> 00:44:07,204
I...

599
00:44:10,404 --> 00:44:12,404
really want to get out of here too,

600
00:44:14,944 --> 00:44:16,514
but I don't know how.

601
00:44:32,994 --> 00:44:34,094
All right. That does it.

602
00:44:37,364 --> 00:44:39,004
I don't share this with just anyone.

603
00:44:40,734 --> 00:44:42,534
Whenever I feel that way, I use an amazing magic spell,

604
00:44:42,534 --> 00:44:43,704
and I'll teach it to you.

605
00:44:56,784 --> 00:45:00,524
Screw you!

606
00:45:00,524 --> 00:45:06,894
Screw you!

607
00:45:07,664 --> 00:45:09,434
Tae Gu, don't do that.

608
00:45:11,704 --> 00:45:12,764
Whenever I go on stage,

609
00:45:12,834 --> 00:45:14,204
there's something I always tell my guys.

610
00:45:15,374 --> 00:45:17,074
If you get scared, you lose.

611
00:45:17,474 --> 00:45:19,044
Don't be scared. What's there to fear?

612
00:45:19,844 --> 00:45:23,074
Whenever you run into crappy people in this crappy world,

613
00:45:23,214 --> 00:45:24,544
just shout, "Screw you,"

614
00:45:25,344 --> 00:45:27,454
right in their faces, and keep on walking.

615
00:45:28,554 --> 00:45:29,684
Still...

616
00:45:30,424 --> 00:45:32,824
How can you say something like that?

617
00:45:33,254 --> 00:45:34,594
It's an eye for an eye in this world.

618
00:45:35,594 --> 00:45:37,494
You have to pay bad people right back in kind.

619
00:45:38,124 --> 00:45:40,464
Try it once. It'll feel so liberating.

620
00:45:41,164 --> 00:45:42,164
Go on, say "screw you."

621
00:45:42,964 --> 00:45:44,104
I can't.

622
00:45:44,534 --> 00:45:45,604
"Screw you."

623
00:45:45,934 --> 00:45:48,034
Follow me. Come over here.

624
00:45:48,104 --> 00:45:50,904
- Don't.
- Screw you!

625
00:45:50,904 --> 00:45:52,204
- Tae Gu, don't.
- Try it.

626
00:45:52,204 --> 00:45:53,444
I'm telling you, you'll feel great once you do.

627
00:45:55,374 --> 00:45:58,944
- Sorry, I'm late.
- Hey, where have you been?

628
00:45:59,044 --> 00:46:01,014
- I just stepped out.
- Get changed first.

629
00:46:01,084 --> 00:46:02,754
After nagging me so much... Darn it.

630
00:46:04,784 --> 00:46:06,024
Hey, isn't this too big?

631
00:46:10,594 --> 00:46:11,664
This is way too big.

632
00:46:12,094 --> 00:46:13,694
Do you want to die? Hold still.

633
00:46:13,764 --> 00:46:15,364
- Are you trying to kill me?
- Stop playing dumb.

634
00:46:15,434 --> 00:46:16,434
Guys.

635
00:46:18,734 --> 00:46:20,804
I think we need to do one more show after this.

636
00:46:46,434 --> 00:46:48,264
(Asura Night Show: Special Stage. You are invited to a private show.)

637
00:46:48,334 --> 00:46:50,034
(Location: Soojung Villa Rooftop, Time: Right Now)

638
00:47:01,244 --> 00:47:03,544
- Hello. We're here...
- To turn your minds...

639
00:47:03,614 --> 00:47:04,944
Into total chaos.

640
00:47:06,214 --> 00:47:07,214
- We're Asura!
- We're Asura!

641
00:47:11,624 --> 00:47:15,024
Now, to our audience members, please take your seats.

642
00:47:15,354 --> 00:47:17,064
- Jun Seo?
- Yes.

643
00:47:21,034 --> 00:47:22,064
This way.

644
00:47:29,904 --> 00:47:31,444
(VIP Seat: Go Eun Young)

645
00:47:31,504 --> 00:47:34,044
Now that everyone is seated,

646
00:47:34,244 --> 00:47:37,914
Asura's special performance will now begin.

647
00:47:38,344 --> 00:47:39,914
Please enjoy the show.

648
00:47:46,594 --> 00:47:48,154
(Woman with a Twist Sound Effect)

649
00:47:52,664 --> 00:47:55,594
Today is my first day on the job. Forget the timid me from yesterday.

650
00:47:55,934 --> 00:47:57,404
I'm going to be reborn as a whole new person.

651
00:47:57,904 --> 00:47:58,934
Let's go.

652
00:47:59,464 --> 00:48:00,474
Let's go.

653
00:48:02,234 --> 00:48:03,774
- Babe, take a seat.
- Welcome.

654
00:48:06,714 --> 00:48:08,674
You're as commanding as ever, babe.

655
00:48:08,874 --> 00:48:13,184
Excuse me, two Solomon's seal teas. Strong like espresso.

656
00:48:16,114 --> 00:48:17,454
Half-shot Solomon's seal.

657
00:48:49,414 --> 00:48:50,454
Wait.

658
00:49:01,234 --> 00:49:02,234
Running away...

659
00:49:05,464 --> 00:49:06,474
means admitting defeat.

660
00:49:18,684 --> 00:49:19,684
Isn't that way too much?

661
00:49:24,654 --> 00:49:27,124
Babe, are you okay?

662
00:49:28,724 --> 00:49:30,464
Oh, seriously.

663
00:49:33,664 --> 00:49:34,664
Kang Tae Gu.

664
00:49:41,134 --> 00:49:42,474
What's with your face?

665
00:49:43,274 --> 00:49:45,144
Hey, do it.

666
00:49:45,444 --> 00:49:48,274
Come on and do it.

667
00:50:49,474 --> 00:50:53,274
Some memories are never forgotten.

668
00:50:55,474 --> 00:50:56,474
However,

669
00:50:57,184 --> 00:50:59,814
they can be painted over with other memories.

670
00:51:31,344 --> 00:51:33,714
The wounds that held me back for years...

671
00:51:35,054 --> 00:51:37,824
melt away powerlessly...

672
00:51:39,754 --> 00:51:41,294
before those silly jokes and gestures.

673
00:51:45,924 --> 00:51:47,564
I'm sure of it this time.

674
00:51:50,804 --> 00:51:51,804
It's a miracle.

675
00:51:54,274 --> 00:51:57,444
A miracle just for me.

676
00:52:06,384 --> 00:52:07,984
Since we're getting off work early,

677
00:52:08,054 --> 00:52:09,854
- shall we all have dinner together?
- Sounds good.

678
00:52:09,854 --> 00:52:12,054
- I'm in.
- Forget dinner. Let's grab drinks.

679
00:52:12,124 --> 00:52:13,924
- Sounds great.
- All right.

680
00:52:13,924 --> 00:52:16,054
Oh, right. Did I tell you guys?

681
00:52:16,294 --> 00:52:17,964
Do you know who I ran into recently?

682
00:52:18,224 --> 00:52:19,934
- Who did you meet?
- Who did you see? A celebrity?

683
00:52:19,934 --> 00:52:22,534
Well, you see, last time...

684
00:52:24,364 --> 00:52:26,264
- Behind you.
- What?

685
00:52:29,174 --> 00:52:30,174
Hello.

686
00:52:31,274 --> 00:52:32,274
Eun Young.

687
00:52:32,804 --> 00:52:34,674
I was just talking about you.

688
00:52:35,544 --> 00:52:36,814
What brings you here, Eun Young?

689
00:52:37,114 --> 00:52:40,054
I came to return the employee badge that I couldn't return back then.

690
00:52:40,614 --> 00:52:41,614
(Go Eun Young)

691
00:52:43,354 --> 00:52:45,954
And I came to get an apology...

692
00:52:47,224 --> 00:52:50,124
for the way you all treated me.

693
00:52:51,294 --> 00:52:52,294
Starting with you, Hee Jin.

694
00:52:53,464 --> 00:52:54,464
- Me?
- Goodness.

695
00:52:56,764 --> 00:52:58,834
Eun Young, you're hilarious today in so many ways.

696
00:52:59,134 --> 00:53:00,134
An apology?

697
00:53:01,234 --> 00:53:02,234
An apology for what?

698
00:53:02,674 --> 00:53:05,644
Eun Young, I don't know why you're suddenly acting like this,

699
00:53:05,974 --> 00:53:07,274
but you should be grateful...

700
00:53:07,344 --> 00:53:10,044
that we didn't say anything about how you ran off back then.

701
00:53:10,384 --> 00:53:12,114
We let it slide only because it was us.

702
00:53:12,114 --> 00:53:13,654
- You know that?
- As expected,

703
00:53:14,884 --> 00:53:17,454
you're all terrible people.

704
00:53:18,454 --> 00:53:22,424
So I'm allowed to do this too.

705
00:53:23,194 --> 00:53:27,134
They say it's an eye for an eye in this world.

706
00:53:28,734 --> 00:53:30,834
- What the?
- Seriously, darn it.

707
00:53:38,504 --> 00:53:40,674
Eun Young, what are you doing right now?

708
00:53:40,744 --> 00:53:41,974
I'm trying to teach you...

709
00:53:42,244 --> 00:53:44,614
how to apologize when you do something wrong...

710
00:53:45,344 --> 00:53:46,784
because none of you seem to know.

711
00:53:49,354 --> 00:53:50,824
Watch closely and learn, Hee Jin.

712
00:53:51,424 --> 00:53:52,984
This is all for your own good.

713
00:53:54,724 --> 00:53:55,724
Crazy woman.

714
00:53:55,894 --> 00:53:57,424
Eun Young, what on earth is...

715
00:53:59,694 --> 00:54:01,094
I'm not finished yet.

716
00:54:02,934 --> 00:54:05,534
I have something to tell you all.

717
00:54:22,454 --> 00:54:23,454
All of you...

718
00:54:27,554 --> 00:54:28,624
can all...

719
00:54:31,764 --> 00:54:37,904
screw yourselves!

720
00:54:37,904 --> 00:54:43,874
screw yourselves!

721
00:54:43,874 --> 00:54:50,284
screw yourselves!

722
00:55:04,124 --> 00:55:06,394
There. Now I'm done.

723
00:55:07,094 --> 00:55:10,904
Excuse me for intruding. I'll take my leave now.

724
00:55:12,364 --> 00:55:13,504
Goodbye.

725
00:55:17,274 --> 00:55:20,274
- What was that?
- Hey, Go Eun Young.

726
00:55:20,274 --> 00:55:21,514
- Hey!
- Eun Young.

727
00:55:24,884 --> 00:55:25,884
All right.

728
00:55:27,454 --> 00:55:30,484
All right. Have a good evening.

729
00:55:35,724 --> 00:55:37,964
- What did he say?
- He said to talk at the theater.

730
00:55:38,164 --> 00:55:39,964
Man, what was all this for, then?

731
00:55:40,024 --> 00:55:41,934
Hey, we ran off in the middle of the night...

732
00:55:42,034 --> 00:55:45,134
with all the lights and mics. CEO Kim has every right to be mad.

733
00:55:45,764 --> 00:55:47,434
Still, how did you even come up with that idea?

734
00:55:48,604 --> 00:55:50,944
Stealing equipment and changing the sketch ending?

735
00:55:51,874 --> 00:55:53,814
Just for fan service.

736
00:55:54,944 --> 00:55:58,014
For the two of us, it was fan service,

737
00:55:59,444 --> 00:56:00,584
but what about you?

738
00:56:01,884 --> 00:56:03,824
Was it really just fan service?

739
00:56:06,024 --> 00:56:07,654
Quit talking nonsense before I...

740
00:56:07,724 --> 00:56:09,554
- Hey, calm down.
- Have you been hit with scallions?

741
00:56:09,624 --> 00:56:11,964
- Playing with food now?
- Put down the scallions.

742
00:56:11,964 --> 00:56:13,494
Want me to play with my fists instead?

743
00:56:13,564 --> 00:56:16,904
- Go ahead. Try it, hit me.
- I did it. I actually did it.

744
00:56:17,434 --> 00:56:20,064
I went right up to them and told them off.

745
00:56:21,974 --> 00:56:23,474
- Really?
- Yes.

746
00:56:23,474 --> 00:56:25,444
I stood tall like this, yelled at the top of my lungs,

747
00:56:25,504 --> 00:56:27,314
and their eyes got as big as saucers.

748
00:56:27,374 --> 00:56:28,614
Their faces turned beet red.

749
00:56:29,444 --> 00:56:31,514
Before walking in, I had so many second thoughts,

750
00:56:31,514 --> 00:56:33,614
but it felt so good once I let it all out.

751
00:56:34,554 --> 00:56:36,814
I felt alive again.

752
00:56:37,354 --> 00:56:38,754
It was like I could finally breathe.

753
00:56:39,724 --> 00:56:40,954
And so...

754
00:56:44,394 --> 00:56:45,464
Good job.

755
00:56:46,224 --> 00:56:47,234
Good for you.

756
00:56:48,934 --> 00:56:50,034
Congratulations, Madam President.

757
00:57:05,744 --> 00:57:06,884
I thought...

758
00:57:08,184 --> 00:57:10,014
you'd never leave your room again.

759
00:57:12,724 --> 00:57:13,924
That's why...

760
00:57:27,074 --> 00:57:28,074
I'm sorry.

761
00:57:31,004 --> 00:57:32,204
I'm so sorry.

762
00:58:02,804 --> 00:58:06,474
(Nam My First)

763
00:58:11,014 --> 00:58:12,014
What are you doing?

764
00:58:13,654 --> 00:58:14,654
You're awake?

765
00:58:15,654 --> 00:58:16,914
I wanted you to sleep a little more.

766
00:58:17,524 --> 00:58:19,154
You didn't sleep a wink during the conference.

767
00:58:19,984 --> 00:58:21,194
You didn't have to do that.

768
00:58:22,724 --> 00:58:24,624
Sorry. It's my fault.

769
00:58:26,494 --> 00:58:28,994
Thanks for the ride. See you at the office tomorrow.

770
00:58:36,074 --> 00:58:37,504
How long will you play dumb?

771
00:58:39,374 --> 00:58:41,044
(Nam My First)

772
00:58:44,984 --> 00:58:46,644
You're the one playing dumb.

773
00:58:47,354 --> 00:58:48,554
Can't you tell...

774
00:58:49,454 --> 00:58:51,254
I'm rejecting you with every fiber of my being?

775
00:58:52,124 --> 00:58:55,354
When I confessed four years ago, remember what you said?

776
00:58:55,654 --> 00:58:57,824
That you were seeing someone with marriage in mind.

777
00:58:58,464 --> 00:59:00,364
So I stepped aside without a fuss.

778
00:59:01,194 --> 00:59:03,594
- And?
- And yet,

779
00:59:04,364 --> 00:59:06,804
you still haven't gotten married.

780
00:59:09,974 --> 00:59:10,974
I will.

781
00:59:11,504 --> 00:59:13,374
- Don't worry about it.
- When?

782
00:59:13,914 --> 00:59:15,314
Has he even proposed?

783
00:59:15,774 --> 00:59:18,384
- Does he even plan to marry you?
- Hey.

784
00:59:19,014 --> 00:59:21,054
- What are you even...
- Na Yeon.

785
00:59:22,614 --> 00:59:23,614
Mom.

786
00:59:26,184 --> 00:59:27,954
Hello, ma'am.

787
00:59:28,654 --> 00:59:30,764
I'm Jung Tae Hoon, Na Yeon's colleague.

788
00:59:33,494 --> 00:59:35,334
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

789
00:59:35,394 --> 00:59:37,164
You should invite your guest upstairs.

790
00:59:37,234 --> 00:59:40,234
- Why are you keeping him out here?
- He's not a guest.

791
00:59:40,534 --> 00:59:42,104
He just dropped me off on his way.

792
00:59:42,934 --> 00:59:44,874
Go on. You said you were tired.

793
00:59:46,104 --> 00:59:47,544
All right. I'll head out.

794
00:59:48,744 --> 00:59:51,044
Ma'am, it's quite late tonight,

795
00:59:51,114 --> 00:59:53,644
so I'll make a proper visit for tea sometime soon.

796
00:59:53,914 --> 00:59:54,954
I'll see you then.

797
00:59:55,384 --> 00:59:56,384
- Get home safely.
- Thank you.

798
00:59:56,914 --> 00:59:59,184
- Do come by for tea.
- Yes, ma'am. I will.

799
01:00:02,824 --> 01:00:05,524
- What are you doing? Let's go.
- Okay.

800
01:00:13,204 --> 01:00:14,274
Is this all?

801
01:00:15,934 --> 01:00:18,744
Yes, we stayed up all night putting it together.

802
01:00:18,804 --> 01:00:21,714
You stayed up all night, so I should shut up and take it?

803
01:00:21,944 --> 01:00:25,384
No, that's not what I meant. It's just that...

804
01:00:25,784 --> 01:00:27,314
chemistry is crucial for this sketch,

805
01:00:27,584 --> 01:00:29,684
so only a team that has worked together for a long time...

806
01:00:29,784 --> 01:00:31,284
can really pull off this kind of comedy.

807
01:00:33,824 --> 01:00:34,824
Hey.

808
01:00:35,054 --> 01:00:36,894
- Yes?
- Get over here.

809
01:00:41,434 --> 01:00:44,104
So what are you really trying to say?

810
01:00:45,104 --> 01:00:46,334
Well...

811
01:00:46,604 --> 01:00:48,134
We took rehearsal time into account when we...

812
01:00:48,204 --> 01:00:49,274
Then you're out.

813
01:00:50,574 --> 01:00:53,814
- Excuse me?
- If you can't do it, get out.

814
01:00:55,244 --> 01:00:58,614
Even without you, plenty of people are dying to join my team.

815
01:00:58,714 --> 01:01:02,214
You said you had family debt to pay, so I cut you slack.

816
01:01:03,584 --> 01:01:05,954
Hey, who do you have to thank...

817
01:01:05,954 --> 01:01:08,324
for getting your vouchers week after week?

818
01:01:08,754 --> 01:01:10,624
Have you all lost your minds?

819
01:01:11,624 --> 01:01:12,624
Hey.

820
01:01:13,724 --> 01:01:14,834
Call Jin Gon.

821
01:01:14,894 --> 01:01:16,694
Tell him I'll give him a regular segment.

822
01:01:17,234 --> 01:01:18,234
What?

823
01:01:21,434 --> 01:01:24,004
- Well...
- Pardon?

824
01:01:24,544 --> 01:01:25,544
Hey, you do it.

825
01:01:25,604 --> 01:01:28,844
- With Jin Gon and one other guy.
- Really? I'll do it.

826
01:01:29,544 --> 01:01:30,784
I'll do it.

827
01:01:34,214 --> 01:01:37,324
Know your place before you act up.

828
01:01:42,054 --> 01:01:43,124
Darn it.

829
01:01:45,894 --> 01:01:48,064
- Good job.
- Thanks for your hard work.

830
01:01:48,434 --> 01:01:49,694
Excuse me, sir.

831
01:01:50,964 --> 01:01:51,964
You scared me.

832
01:01:52,604 --> 01:01:53,934
Were you waiting for me?

833
01:01:55,934 --> 01:01:56,934
Yes.

834
01:01:58,144 --> 01:02:01,044
Well, the thing is...

835
01:02:01,974 --> 01:02:04,344
There's something I need to tell you.

836
01:02:06,144 --> 01:02:07,144
Yes?

837
01:02:09,054 --> 01:02:10,654
One of his own teammates reported it.

838
01:02:10,854 --> 01:02:12,424
I think we need to call him in and check.

839
01:02:12,884 --> 01:02:13,894
Look,

840
01:02:13,954 --> 01:02:16,254
it's obvious. It's 100 percent true.

841
01:02:16,494 --> 01:02:17,494
Hwang Chan Sung...

842
01:02:17,564 --> 01:02:19,164
has pulled this kind of stunt a few times before.

843
01:02:20,024 --> 01:02:22,694
Man, but if the bastard is going to play dirty,

844
01:02:22,764 --> 01:02:24,634
he should at least cover his tracks properly.

845
01:02:24,704 --> 01:02:28,304
He's just dumb enough to always get rumors started.

846
01:02:33,404 --> 01:02:34,414
What?

847
01:02:34,844 --> 01:02:36,214
Sir... I mean, Director.

848
01:02:36,744 --> 01:02:38,514
It makes no sense to just look the other way.

849
01:02:38,584 --> 01:02:41,014
Isn't this basically theft?

850
01:02:41,084 --> 01:02:43,054
How many times do I have to tell you?

851
01:02:43,114 --> 01:02:46,184
What matters more than being right is ratings.

852
01:02:46,454 --> 01:02:50,054
Be realistic. Between a bunch of complete nobodies...

853
01:02:50,124 --> 01:02:52,524
and Hwang Chan Sung, who benefits us more?

854
01:02:52,594 --> 01:02:54,164
Can you really not figure that out?

855
01:02:54,764 --> 01:02:57,934
Good grief... Am I talking to a wall here?

856
01:03:06,574 --> 01:03:07,674
(Producer Park Chae Rin)

857
01:03:07,744 --> 01:03:09,044
(Urgent! Hwang Chan Sung Street Fight Video)

858
01:03:12,914 --> 01:03:14,554
The moment you stole my work,

859
01:03:16,754 --> 01:03:18,254
you lost to me for the rest of your life.

860
01:03:23,724 --> 01:03:26,794
(Urgent! Hwang Chan Sung Street Fight Video)

861
01:03:28,734 --> 01:03:29,734
No way.

862
01:03:29,794 --> 01:03:32,904
- Hey. Did you guys see this?
- See what?

863
01:03:32,964 --> 01:03:34,404
(Urgent! Hwang Chan Sung Street Fight Video)

864
01:03:34,604 --> 01:03:36,474
- No way.
- Holy crap.

865
01:03:36,534 --> 01:03:38,474
Oh, my gosh, what's this?

866
01:03:39,944 --> 01:03:41,274
(Urgent! Hwang Chan Sung Street Fight Video)

867
01:03:41,344 --> 01:03:42,374
Seriously...

868
01:03:42,944 --> 01:03:44,314
(Is this real or fake? His face looks real.)

869
01:03:45,814 --> 01:03:47,214
(I liked Hwang Chan Sung, but this ruined him.)

870
01:03:47,284 --> 01:03:48,584
(So that's why people talked about his rep.)

871
01:03:48,654 --> 01:03:50,554
(170,199 Views)

872
01:03:50,624 --> 01:03:51,954
(Who's next to him? Hwang's image is trashed.)

873
01:03:52,024 --> 01:03:53,424
(PR can't hide your true colors.)

874
01:03:55,954 --> 01:03:58,124
What's this? You're ready already?

875
01:03:58,324 --> 01:04:00,364
Of course, we have to get to the meeting.

876
01:04:00,524 --> 01:04:01,834
You guys hurry up and get ready too.

877
01:04:02,094 --> 01:04:03,864
Wait, hold on, stop.

878
01:04:04,734 --> 01:04:06,464
Why are you being so extra this morning?

879
01:04:07,104 --> 01:04:08,434
- What?
- Did you put product in your hair?

880
01:04:08,504 --> 01:04:09,504
- No, I didn't.
- Hey.

881
01:04:10,174 --> 01:04:12,374
What's with you? What's this smell?

882
01:04:12,604 --> 01:04:14,614
- Did you put on cologne?
- It's just fresh laundry...

883
01:04:14,674 --> 01:04:16,814
- How much detergent did this guy...
- Hey, did you put that out...

884
01:04:16,814 --> 01:04:19,684
for recycling? Look, I'll take care of it,

885
01:04:19,744 --> 01:04:21,054
so just throw something on and come out.

886
01:04:21,254 --> 01:04:23,354
- "Throw something on"?
- Just come out as you are.

887
01:04:26,524 --> 01:04:28,694
Stupid wind, darn it...

888
01:04:29,554 --> 01:04:31,164
Give me a break. You look fine.

889
01:04:32,724 --> 01:04:34,764
It's really nothing like that.

890
01:04:35,734 --> 01:04:36,794
Sure it isn't.

891
01:04:37,534 --> 01:04:38,834
Touchy today, aren't we?

892
01:04:42,174 --> 01:04:43,174
Hello.

893
01:04:47,444 --> 01:04:48,444
Hey.

894
01:04:49,614 --> 01:04:52,044
What was that just now? Was it just me?

895
01:04:53,144 --> 01:04:54,154
No.

896
01:04:55,084 --> 01:04:56,654
I think we felt it too.

897
01:04:57,384 --> 01:04:58,484
Do you know him?

898
01:04:58,754 --> 01:04:59,754
No.

899
01:05:01,154 --> 01:05:03,794
- Do I have a booger?
- It's Asura.

900
01:05:05,124 --> 01:05:06,994
- Nope.
- Asura?

901
01:05:07,864 --> 01:05:09,364
It's Asura!

902
01:05:10,364 --> 01:05:11,764
What? How do they know us?

903
01:05:12,064 --> 01:05:15,134
(Solhan Elementary School)

904
01:05:15,704 --> 01:05:18,304
Mister, why did you fight Hwang Chan Sung?

905
01:05:18,504 --> 01:05:20,444
- What?
- Are you good at fighting, mister?

906
01:05:20,444 --> 01:05:21,444
- Well, no...
- Mister,

907
01:05:21,444 --> 01:05:23,974
- what did Hwang Chan Sung steal?
- What?

908
01:05:24,314 --> 01:05:25,514
What's he talking about?

909
01:05:26,614 --> 01:05:28,014
- I have no idea.
- Let's get autographs.

910
01:05:28,084 --> 01:05:30,084
Autographs. Please give us an autograph.

911
01:05:30,154 --> 01:05:33,124
- Okay, okay, calm down.
- Give us an autograph.

912
01:05:33,184 --> 01:05:36,854
You're going to get hurt, okay? Quiet down, everyone. Zip your lips.

913
01:05:36,924 --> 01:05:39,224
- It's Asura.
- It's Asura!

914
01:05:39,294 --> 01:05:42,134
- It's Asura.
- It's really Asura.

915
01:05:42,194 --> 01:05:43,194
It's Asura.

916
01:05:43,734 --> 01:05:46,204
- No, it's not.
- Yes, it is.

917
01:05:46,704 --> 01:05:48,674
- It's Asura.
- No, it's not.

918
01:05:48,734 --> 01:05:49,734
Yes, it is.

919
01:06:00,584 --> 01:06:02,254
- It's Asura.
- Hey, run.

920
01:06:09,624 --> 01:06:10,964
It's Asura!

921
01:06:12,524 --> 01:06:13,824
It's Asura!

922
01:06:20,504 --> 01:06:21,534
What in the world...

923
01:06:27,674 --> 01:06:28,844
Give us an autograph.

924
01:06:32,244 --> 01:06:34,114
- Hurry up.
- Give us an autograph.

925
01:06:34,254 --> 01:06:35,484
Give us an autograph.

926
01:06:47,834 --> 01:06:51,604
(Happy Anding)

927
01:06:51,734 --> 01:06:53,764
We decided to have you join us starting next season.

928
01:06:53,904 --> 01:06:54,904
An interview?

929
01:06:54,974 --> 01:06:57,604
Everyone is buzzing about who Asura is.

930
01:06:58,174 --> 01:06:59,804
You guys look like real celebrities now.

931
01:06:59,874 --> 01:07:01,074
We don't just look like celebrities.

932
01:07:01,144 --> 01:07:02,844
We've been celebrities all along.

933
01:07:02,914 --> 01:07:04,644
That's always your problem, man.

934
01:07:04,744 --> 01:07:07,654
- Hey, if you like her, make a move.
- I don't know.

935
01:07:07,714 --> 01:07:09,054
She's not even interested in me.

936
01:07:09,054 --> 01:07:11,154
Nobody is here.

937
01:07:11,624 --> 01:07:13,124
Why do you keep taking your anger out on me?

938
01:07:13,184 --> 01:07:16,194
- I don't know either.
- Do you have feelings for me?

939
01:07:16,254 --> 01:07:18,394
(Generative AI Used In Select Scenes)
